                        "sense_id": "dae87384-076d-3e29-9a0f-074b791494c4",
                        "entry_id": "df249386-6c3e-3688-9ce8-ed7eafa27b0d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A long-lived blind soothsayer who participated over seven generations in the legendary history of (the Greek city) Thebes, noted also for being transformed into a woman for seven years, so being symbolic of androgyny."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Greek"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efef6b93-040a-45fb-9a2e-1cdb1c300a39",
                                "sense_id": "dae87384-076d-3e29-9a0f-074b791494c4",
                                "text": "[…]somewhere a ship's radio was blaring out the latest jazz-hit to reach Alexandria:\nOld Tiresias / No one half so breezy as, / Half so free and easy as / Old Tiresias."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f08be4d1-e4ba-4d2e-b0a3-ea0a31a66020",
                                "sense_id": "dae87384-076d-3e29-9a0f-074b791494c4",
                                "text": "The myth associated with how Tiresias became a hermaphrodite reveals much about relations between the sexes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
